<section class="hero">
	<div class="wrap hero-content">
		<h1>Make your MacBook's notch actually useful.</h1>
		<p class="subhead">
			DynamicNotch turns the notch into a live system dashboard — music controls, fan
			speeds, CPU stats, audio visualization, and smart HUD replacements, all in the
			space that was doing nothing.
		</p>
		<div class="cta-row">
			<a
				class="btn btn-primary"
				href="https://github.com/Hitjack007/DynamicNotch/releases/latest"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener"
			>
				Download for macOS
			</a>
			<a
				class="btn btn-secondary"
				href="https://github.com/Hitjack007/DynamicNotch"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener"
			>
				View on GitHub
			</a>
		</div>
		<p class="req">macOS 15 Sequoia or later &middot; works even without a physical notch display</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.hero {
		position: relative;
		height: 92vh;
		min-height: 620px;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
	}

	.hero-content {
		position: relative;
		text-align: center;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 22px;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: clamp(34px, 6vw, 64px);
		font-weight: 700;
		line-height: 1.05;
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 820px;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		text-shadow: 0 2px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
	}

	.subhead {
		font-size: clamp(16px, 2vw, 20px);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: rgba(245, 245, 247, 0.78);
		max-width: 640px;
		margin: 0;
		text-shadow: 0 1px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.6);
	}

	.cta-row {
		display: flex;
		gap: 14px;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		justify-content: center;
		margin-top: 6px;
	}

	.req {
		font-size: 14px;
		color: rgba(245, 245, 247, 0.55);
		margin: 4px 0 0;
	}
</style>
